+## beforeSession failure guarantees
+
+- When `beforeSession` throws, `onError` fires with the thrown error, the same as for any other failure in the turn ([validated by: onError fires when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L32)).
+- When `beforeSession` throws, `afterSession` fires, so a hook that allocated a resource in `beforeSession` can release it even on failure; the hook receives the session as it existed when `beforeSession` was called, with none of the later lifecycle hooks having run ([validated by: afterSession fires when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L50)).
+
 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
 These three properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` are recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue changes none of them; each is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
